---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import QuickAnswer from '../../../components/QuickAnswer.astro';
import LastVerified from '../../../components/LastVerified.astro';
import SourceList from '../../../components/SourceList.astro';
import RelatedGuides from '../../../components/RelatedGuides.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../../../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import CTASection from '../../../components/CTASection.astro';
import { sourceUrls } from '../../../data/sources';

const title = 'DragonSword Awakening Beginner Guide — First Hours & Combat Basics';
const description = 'A practical DragonSword Awakening beginner guide covering first-hours progression, tag combat, early teams, exploration, Cooking, Familiars, and safe upgrade habits.';
const canonical = 'https://dragonswordguide.com/guides/beginner/';
const article = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: title, description, mainEntityOfPage: canonical, datePublished: '2026-08-08', dateModified: '2026-08-08', publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'DragonSword Guide' } };
const sources = [{ label: 'Official Steam store page', href: sourceUrls.steam, note: 'supports Orbis, companions, Cooking, Familiars, Status Ailments, Signal Skills and 19 Heroes.' }];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} ogType="article" schema={[article]}>
  <div class="shell page-wrap"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'DragonSword Guide', href: '/' }, { label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/beginner/' }, { label: 'Beginner Guide' }]} /><article><header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow">Guide · First hours</p><h1>DragonSword Awakening Beginner Guide</h1><LastVerified date="August 8, 2026" /></header>
    <QuickAnswer title="Learn the combat loop before spending materials."><p>Start by understanding Active Skills, Status Ailments, Signal Skills and team switching. Build one functional three-Hero team, explore at your pace, and keep limited upgrade materials for characters you have actually tested.</p></QuickAnswer>
    <div class="article-body"><SectionHeader title="First-hours checklist" description="A low-regret route for a new save." /><ul class="checklist"><li>Complete the opening tutorials and read the combat prompts.</li><li>Practice dodge, camera control and switching before chasing damage.</li><li>Learn how Active Skills apply or use Status Ailments.</li><li>Use Signal Skills after the relevant ailment setup.</li><li>Keep one functional three-Hero team before splitting resources.</li><li>Follow story progression, then return for caves, cellars and side content.</li><li>Cook when you have ingredients; treat recipes as part of progression, not decoration.</li><li>Experiment with Familiars and note what each one changes for your route.</li><li>Install the game on an SSD; Steam lists an SSD as strictly required for an optimal experience.</li></ul>
      <h2>What to do first</h2><p>DragonSword: Awakening introduces an open world, companions and tag-team combat at the same time. Resist the urge to optimize every system immediately. Your first useful milestone is a team that can reliably create a Status Ailment and convert it into a Signal Skill.</p>
      <h2>Your first combat chain</h2><p>Use an Active Skill, watch for the Status Ailment it creates, then switch into the Hero whose Signal Skill can capitalize on the opening. The official store description supports this broad chain; exact character-specific rotations remain outside this guide until tested in-game.</p>
      <h2>Early team building</h2><p>Think in roles rather than a tier list: a setup Hero, a connector who can exploit the status state, and a finisher. Team order matters because switching is part of the combat language, not just a way to escape danger.</p>
      <h2>Exploration and progression</h2><p>Orbis includes meadows, watchtower cellars, deep seas, caves and dungeons. Mark places you cannot finish yet and return after story or system progress; this keeps exploration useful without pretending every location has been mapped here.</p>
      <h2>Early mistakes to avoid</h2><ul><li>Do not spend every rare material before testing a Hero.</li><li>Do not treat an unverified community tier list as official data.</li><li>Do not assume story or open-world co-op from the store’s Online Co-op label.</li><li>Do not skip the SSD requirement when troubleshooting performance.</li></ul>
      <h2>What to learn next</h2><p>Continue with the <a href="/guides/combat-system/">combat system guide</a>, then use the <a href="/teams/">teams hub</a> and <a href="/map/">map reference</a> once your first team is stable.</p>
    </div><SourceList sources={sources} /><RelatedGuides links={[{ label: 'Combat System', href: '/guides/combat-system/' }, { label: 'Teams', href: '/teams/' }, { label: 'Map', href: '/map/' }]} /><CTASection title="Ready for the combat loop?" primaryHref="/guides/combat-system/" primaryLabel="Read Combat System" secondaryHref="/multiplayer/" secondaryLabel="See Multiplayer" /></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .page-wrap { padding: 1.25rem 0 2rem; } .article-header { max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; } .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-light); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; } h1, h2 { line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.04em; } h1 { max-width: 760px; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 5rem); margin: 0 0 0.7rem; } h2 { font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2rem); margin: 2.8rem 0 0.75rem; } .article-body { max-width: 760px; } .article-body p, li { color: var(--muted-strong); } .checklist { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.65rem 2rem; padding-left: 1.1rem; } li { padding-left: 0.25rem; } @media (max-width: 650px) { .checklist { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
